{% lede %}
With Prof. Bill Hammack at the University of Illinois, I made short videos that explain how ordinary objects are engineered: a beverage can, a ballpoint pen, a music box. The aluminum can video has 19 million views.
{% /lede %}

I co-wrote, directed, filmed, illustrated and edited the videos.

## Illustration

Where the camera couldn't see inside a mechanism, the videos use illustration and animation to show how the parts move, like the cutaway of the retractable pen.

Top: "The Ingenious Design of the Aluminum Beverage Can" (2015), 19 million views, and "How a Retractable Ballpoint Pen Works" (2015), 1.5 million views. View counts as of April 2026.
